From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sysdeps-unix: drop supplementary groups only when running as root

dbus.service starts dbus-daemon with User=dbus. Built without libaudit,
_dbus_change_to_daemon_user() still calls setgroups(), which fails with
EPERM for an unprivileged process and logs at every boot:

  dbus-daemon: Failed to drop supplementary groups: Operation not permitted

Only call setgroups() when the effective UID is 0, as the libaudit
implementation in bus/audit.c already does.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
--- a/dbus/dbus-sysdeps-util-unix.c	2025-02-27 17:29:06.000000000 +0100
+++ b/dbus/dbus-sysdeps-util-unix.c	2026-09-26 10:13:19.453805897 +0200
@@ -353,8 +353,13 @@
    *
    * not sure this is right, maybe if setuid()
    * is going to work then setgroups() should also work.
+   *
+   * When systemd already started us as the bus user (User= in
+   * dbus.service), there are no supplementary groups to drop and the
+   * call can only fail with EPERM, so skip it, as the libaudit variant
+   * in bus/audit.c does.
    */
-  if (setgroups (0, NULL) < 0)
+  if (_dbus_geteuid () == 0 && setgroups (0, NULL) < 0)
     _dbus_warn ("Failed to drop supplementary groups: %s",
                 _dbus_strerror (errno));
 
